{"availability":"available","full":"Zeptaz/hutch_resolve","name":"hutch_resolve","description":"hutch resolve: a customer complain resolution engine built for hutch","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-01T20:42:08Z","updated":"2026-10-04T08:10:38Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://hutch-resolve.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://resolve.zeptaz.com/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:17.064Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:17.064Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:17.064Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:16:17.064Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Evidence-backed AI resolution for telecom customer complaints.","All data in this repository is synthetic. No HUTCH system, API, credential or real customer record is used or connected."],"features":["Four complaint types, six seeded cases (A–F): balance/recharge deduction (A), data depletion (B), no internet with an active package (C), balance conflict (D), payment captured but not credited (E), VAS dispute without…","Eleven seeded lines (fixture v3): lines 0007–0011 add a partly explained deduction (records explain LKR 73 of a reported LKR 100), a duplicate package renewal, heavy calling with a failed top-up, bonus, transfer and fee…","Exact reconciliation in integer cents (e.g. 1,000 − 499 − 60 − 21 = 420); quota and money kept in separate calculations.","Balance reconstruction: opening balance + recharges, bonuses and refunds − calls, SMS, data, packages, VAS, transfers and fees = expected balance, from ledger postings and itemised usage, compared with the recorded…","Escalation only when justified: an explained balance is proved with its breakdown; a human review is offered for unexplained money or missing evidence, or when the customer asks. Chat shows the full breakdown, Voice…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Zeptaz/hutch_resolve/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"020d110afc93d113235cd8f55a035b78f2dc1577e5ad4b970ae2c2b866b1dda5","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:58.032Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:58.032Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Evidence-backed AI resolution for telecom customer complaints.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Zeptaz/hutch_resolve/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Requirements: Docker Desktop, Python 3.12, Node.js 20.19+ or 22.12+ with npm (required by Vite 8), and a Google Gemini API key (paid tier recommended; the free tier runs out of quota quickly).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Zeptaz/hutch_resolve/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Demo sign-in stays disabled until DEMOIDENTITIESJSON holds credential hashes; the demo identities are shared separately with the judges.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Zeptaz/hutch_resolve/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"Suggested demo: case A (balance deduction → evidence → stop VAS → Trust Receipt), then case D (LKR 70 conflict → no account change → review ticket in /agent).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Zeptaz/hutch_resolve/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"020d110afc93d113235cd8f55a035b78f2dc1577e5ad4b970ae2c2b866b1dda5","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Zeptaz/hutch_resolve/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:58.032Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T08:10:38Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Zeptaz/hutch_resolve/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:58.033Z","hash":"020d110afc93d113235cd8f55a035b78f2dc1577e5ad4b970ae2c2b866b1dda5","originalBytes":18608,"storedBytes":18608,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["voice","resolve","api","demo","gemini","frontend","hutch","service","agent","backend","balance","run","crm","customer","only","conversation","live","package","chat","database","docs","hubspot","python","syn